8|0@science^1440878572#cuk0ot2:blaaaahhhhh$:Agreed... I didnt even realise what I was eating was too much Started dieting about 4 months ago properly using myfitness pal. As a starting point, I cut down my regular meals to half of what i would usually eat. Then I aimed for 400-600 calories per meal, which in turn forced me to eat healthier so I could be more full after each meal (fresh made chicken chow mein/spag bol etc is far, far less calories than convenience food that isn't filling) Now i'm on track with healthy eating, exercise and over 30lbs down, even the half meals seem too big I used to wof down 4-5k calories a day and think it was normal... Only when i tracked it did i see how bad it was Aim between 1200-1700 now with 30-60mins cardio every day and weights 3 times a week Can't believe how much I used to eat The my fitness pal app is a must for anyone trying to get healthier. Even if just to identify problems. I started using it with my regular diet at first and was shocked by my calorie intake
