-7|0@science^1440870874#cujwn5c:ashlex11$:Theres Low density lipoprotein ( LDL) that can be VLDL( very low density lipoproteins) or LDL( low density lipoproteins), and the LDLs are what contribute to cholesterol. I think you are thinking about High Density Lipoproteins (HDL) . The HDLs go around picking up cholesterol from the bloodstream and get it out of there. High HDLs can lower the amount of LDLs and in turn lower cholesterol. But saturated fat is more associated with LDLs ( bad kind). So yes, a diet rich in saturated fats can lower the HDL and can raise LDL. Tldr; yes. Saturated fats raise LDL ( bad ) levels and do not improve the HDL ( good) levels.
