0|0@science^1440997032#culj2ue:billsil$:&gt; insaturated Unsaturated, not insaturated &gt; saturated oils are harder to break than insaturated oils. Oleic acid (18:1; think olive oil) is much longer than lauric acid (12:0; think coconut oil. In fact, stearic acid (18:0; most beef fat) breaks down into oleic acid, and such that it doesn't even raise cholesterol levels. Also, you're suggesting saturated fats have more calories per gram than unsaturated fats. That's simply not true. I'm calling source. 
